## Apps created with the Deno Slack SDK {#workflow-apps}

[Apps created with the Deno Slack SDK](https://docs.slack.dev/tools/deno-slack-sdk.md) also have an admin approval process, and can have workflows added to them after approval. Those workflows still need to respect the approved scopes discussed above. For more information about the admin approval process for these apps, refer to [admin approval](https://docs.slack.dev/tools/deno-slack-sdk/guides/controlling-permissions-for-admins.md#approval-admins).

* * *

### IP allowlist {#ip-allowlist}

If your app has [allowed IP address ranges](https://docs.slack.dev/concepts/security.md#verify) configured, requests to the Slack MCP server are subject to the same restrictions. API calls originating from IP addresses not on your allowlist will be rejected. Ensure that the IP addresses your MCP client uses are included in your app's allowed list.

* * *

## Apps created with the Deno Slack SDK {#workflow-apps}

[Apps created with the Deno Slack SDK](https://docs.slack.dev/tools/deno-slack-sdk.md) also have an admin approval process, and can have workflows added to them after approval. Those workflows still need to respect the approved scopes discussed above. For more information about the admin approval process for these apps, refer to [admin approval](https://docs.slack.dev/tools/deno-slack-sdk/guides/controlling-permissions-for-admins.md#approval-admins).

