### Beware of is_shared {#is_shared}

The property `is_shared` on a [conversation object](https://docs.slack.dev/reference/objects/conversation-object.md) means the channel is shared with one or more workspaces. But beware: these can be internal workspaces (as with multi-workspace channels in Enterprise organizations) or external workspaces (as with Slack Connect).

Look for `is_ext_shared` and `is_org_shared` to learn which kind of shared channel you're viewing.

## Managing your app's Slack Connect invitations {#managing-app-invitations}

Your app can be invited to a Slack Connect Channel. Use the [`shared_channel_invite_received`](https://docs.slack.dev/reference/events/shared_channel_invite_received.md) event to be notified when suitors call.

The `shared_channel_invite_received` event is fired when a shared channel invite was sent. This event will fire **only** if the [`conversations.inviteShared`](https://docs.slack.dev/reference/methods/conversations.inviteshared.md) API method is called to invite an app to a Slack Connect channel.

