### Search capabilities {#search-capabilities}

The Real-time Search API supports both keyword and semantic retrieval. Refer to the [search capabilities](https://docs.slack.dev/apis/web-api/real-time-search-api.md#search-capabilities) section of the usage guide for details on how each mode works and when each is triggered.

The `sort` parameter influences which retrieval mode is used. Semantic retrieval applies only with the default relevance sort (`sort` set to `score`). Setting `sort` to `timestamp` uses keyword retrieval, which can return a different set of matching messages, not just the same results in a different order.

